## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of lock-free inter-process communication under simple multicore constraints and cache coherence protocols. It distinguishes candidates who know the mechanics of atomics from those who understand visibility and ordering guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free ring buffers with atomic indices
- Acquire/release semantics for safe cross-core visibility
- Wrap-around via power-of-two masking
- Contention handling and backoff strategies

## Code Example
```c
#define SIZE 1024  // power of two
#define MASK (SIZE - 1)

_Atomic size_t head = 0;
_Atomic size_t tail = 0;
type_t buffer[SIZE];

void enqueue(type_t value) {
    size_t h = atomic_fetch_add(&head, 1, memory_order_relaxed);
    buffer[h & MASK] = value;
    atomic_thread_fence(memory_order_release);
}

type_t dequeue(void) {
    size_t t = atomic_load(&tail, memory_order_acquire);
    type_t value = buffer[t & MASK];
    atomic_fetch_add(&tail, 1, memory_order_relaxed);
    return value;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests IPC basics, race-free data sharing, and practical use of CAS and memory barriers in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Lock-free synchronization
- Atomic operations and memory ordering
- Ring buffer wraparound
- Empty/full conditions and visibility

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct { atomic_uint head, tail; Message buf[N]; } Channel;

bool send(Channel *c, Message m){
  unsigned long t = atomic_load_explicit(&c->tail, memory_order_relaxed);
  unsigned long w = (t + 1) % N;
  if (w == atomic_load_explicit(&c->head, memory_order_acquire)) return false; // full
  while (!atomic_compare_exchange_weak(&c->tail, &t, w, memory_order_acq_rel, memory_order_relaxed));
  c->buf[t] = m;
  atomic_thread_fence(memory_order_release);
  return true;
}

bool recv(Channel *c, Message *out){
  unsigned long h;
  do {
    h = atomic_load_explicit(&c->head, memory_order_relaxed);
    if (h == atomic_load_explicit(&c->tail, memory_order_acquire)) return false; // empty
  } while (!atomic_compare_exchange_weak(&c->head, &h, (h+1)%N, memory_order_acq_rel, memory_order_relaxed));
  *out = c->buf[h];
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add a timeout or backoff when the buffer is full/empty?
- How would you adapt this for multiple producers or consumers without locks?

